cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GuidedWaveFEM in academic research or industrial applications, please cite it as below."
title: "GuidedWaveFEM: Unified Guided & Surface Wave Finite Element Framework"
type: software
abstract: >-
  GuidedWaveFEM is an MPI-parallel finite element framework built on DOLFINx and
  PETSc for simulating elastic guided and surface waves (Lamb, Rayleigh, leaky and
  interface waves) in layered plates and halfspaces with isotropic, anisotropic,
  viscoelastic and regularized fluid layers. It provides a rigorously stable
  lumped-mass explicit RK4 solver, an implicit Newmark solver, absorbing sponge
  layers, exact point sensors and 2D FFT dispersion analysis from seismic to
  ultrasonic scales.
authors:
  - family-names: "Le"
    given-names: "Ductho"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ductho-le/GuidedWaveFEM"
keywords:
